<article class="article-wrap">
  <div class="article-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="article-tag">QR Code</div>
      <h1>WhatsApp QR Codes for Restaurant Menus: Complete Guide</h1>
      <div class="article-meta"><span>Jun 23, 2026</span><span>·</span><span>4 min read</span></div>
      <p class="article-intro">Ditch paper menus and complex ordering portals. A simple WhatsApp QR code at tables lets diners view your menu, ask questions, and place orders directly with your staff.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="container">
    <div class="prose">
      <div class="callout"><strong>Quick start:</strong> Generate a WhatsApp link with the message "Hi! I want to view today's menu" using <a href="/">LinkWA</a>, and download the free QR code to print on your table standees.</div>

      <h2>The restaurant menu problem</h2>
      <p>Traditional print menus are expensive to modify, wear out quickly, and cannot easily display seasonal specials. On the other hand, complex digital ordering applications require users to download apps or fill in multiple fields, creating friction. A WhatsApp QR code offers a elegant middle ground. Customers scan the QR, and the system sends the menu as a PDF or link instantly, starting a personal interaction.</p>

      <h2>How WhatsApp menu QR codes work</h2>
      <p>Implementing a WhatsApp menu QR code is simple. Follow these steps:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Generate the code:</strong> Create a WhatsApp link that triggers a pre-filled message like "Hi, please send me the menu for [Restaurant Name]".</li>
        <li><strong>Automate the response:</strong> Configure an automated auto-reply in your WhatsApp Business app. When a user sends that message, the app immediately sends the menu PDF or link.</li>
        <li><strong>Print and place:</strong> Print the QR code on small cards or standees and place them at tables, bar counters, or display windows.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Benefits of WhatsApp Menus for Restaurants</h2>
      <h3>1. Instantly collect customer contact details</h3>
      <p>Unlike standard PDF menus, when customers scan a WhatsApp QR code, they send a message to your business number. This allows you to save their contact details, send promotional offers, share seasonal menus, and run loyalty campaigns directly.</p>

      <h3>2. Easy menu updates</h3>
      <p>If you need to change a price or add a dish, you don't need to reprint anything. Simply update the PDF or web link attached to your automated WhatsApp auto-reply. The QR code on your tables remains exactly the same.</p>

      <h3>3. Better customer service</h3>
      <p>Dinners can ask questions about allergens, request recommendations, or call a server directly within the chat. This personal connection increases customer satisfaction and average order value.</p>

      <h2>Designing and printing your QR standees</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Size:</strong> Print the QR code at least 5cm × 5cm to ensure customers can scan it easily under various lighting conditions.</li>
        <li><strong>Contrast:</strong> Keep the background white or light green so phone cameras can quickly scan the QR.</li>
        <li><strong>Call to action:</strong> Clearly state "Scan here to view menu and order on WhatsApp" next to the code.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="article-cta">
      <h3>Generate your restaurant QR code</h3>
